[Event "Englund Gambit"]
[Opening "Englund Gambit"]
[ECO "A40"]
[Origin "Fritz Englund (early 1900s)"]
[Side "black"]
[Tags "d4,gambit,offbeat,trap"]
[Difficulty "1"]

1. d4 e5 { The Englund Gambit: a provocative pawn offer aiming for quick tricks. }
2. dxe5 Nc6 { Attacking the e5 pawn at once. }
3. Nf3 Qe7 { Piling up on e5 and preparing the famous trap. }
4. Bf4 Qb4+ { Check that also forks the f4 bishop and b2. }
5. Bd2 Qxb2 { Taking the pawn; now 6.Bc3? walks into a mating net. }
6. Bc3 { [%name 6.Bc3? Trap] }
( 6. Nc3 { [%name 6.Nc3 Main Line] }
  6... Bb4 { Pinning the knight; the threat is ...Bxc3 winning material. }
  7. Rb1 Qa3 8. Rb3 Qa5 { The queen escapes and keeps the pin; Black will win back e5 with ...Nge7 and ...Ng6. } )
6... Bb4 { Pinning the bishop so the queen can't be defended from c3. }
7. Qd2 Bxc3 8. Qxc3 Qc1# { The Englund trap: the queen mates on c1. } *
